.TH LOGGLY 1 "2026-11-24" "Loggly SDK 4.0.0"
.SH NAME
loggly \- portable Loggly API clients
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B loggly
.RI [ --dry-run ]
.I command
.RI [ arguments ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Shell, Python, Lua and Nushell implementations share this command contract. API responses are raw bytes. Local discovery needs no credentials.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B "search q=QUERY [from=TIME] [until=TIME] [order=asc/desc] [size=N]"
Legacy/deprecated. Create a search and return its result identifier (RSID); use events to retrieve it. Prefer iterate for new workflows.
.TP
.B "events rsid=ID [page=N] [format=json/raw/csv] [columns=CSV]"
Legacy/deprecated. Retrieve a page from a search RSID. JSON is the default; raw and CSV are also available. Legacy search retrieval is limited to 5000 events.
.TP
.B "iterate [q=QUERY] [from=TIME] [until=TIME] [size=N] [order=asc/desc]"
Search and retrieve the first page in one call. Follow next within ten minutes if present.
.TP
.B "next URL"
Retrieve the next iterator page using an unmodified same-account pagination URL.
.TP
.B "count [q=QUERY] [from=TIME] [until=TIME] [include_volume=true/false]"
Count matching events; optionally retrieve their combined volume in bytes.
.TP
.B "fields [q=QUERY] [from=TIME] [until=TIME] [facet_size=N]"
List parsed field names matching a search; maximum 500 fields.
.TP
.B "field FIELD [q=QUERY] [from=TIME] [until=TIME] [facet_size=N]"
Retrieve values and occurrence counts for one parsed field; maximum 300 values.
.TP
.B "stats TYPE FIELD [q=QUERY] [from=TIME] [until=TIME]"
Compute statistics for a numeric indexed field. Requires an eligible Enterprise subscription.
.TP
.B "usage from=TIME until=TIME [group_by=VALUE ...] [host=VALUE ...] [app=VALUE ...] [measurement_types=VALUE ...]"
Retrieve log volume and event counts, optionally grouped and filtered.
.TP
.B "customer"
Retrieve account information, including sensitive ingestion tokens. Do not include its output in agent context unnecessarily.
.TP
.B "users"
Retrieve active account users; output may contain personal information.
.TP
.B "send - TAGS CONTENT_TYPE < FILE"
Submit one event, including multiline text or JSON. Documented maximum event size is 1 MB.
.TP
.B "bulk - TAGS CONTENT_TYPE < FILE"
Submit newline-separated events. Documented maximum batch size is 5 MB and 1 MB per event.
.TP
.B "pixel - [--tags TAGS] [key=value ...] > pixel.gif"
Submit log data through a tracking pixel GET request. Standard output contains GIF bytes, not JSON.
.TP
.B "request METHOD /PATH [key=value ...] [< BODY]"
Call an additional same-account API path. POST, PUT and PATCH send stdin as JSON; supply their query in the path. HEAD returns headers. Other output depends on the endpoint.
.SH DISCOVERY
.B loggly help [COMMAND]
.br
.B loggly tools
.br
.B loggly schema COMMAND
.br
.B loggly version
.br
.B loggly doctor
.br
.B loggly examples [COMMAND]
.br
.B loggly completion bash|zsh|fish|nu
.br
.B loggly skill list
.br
.B loggly skill show [RESOURCE]
.SH ENVIRONMENT
LOGGLY_API_TOKEN and LOGGLY_SUBDOMAIN are required for every API call. Ingestion also requires LOGGLY_CUSTOMER_TOKEN when using the hyphen token sentinel. Doctor reports configuration booleans only. Dry-run validates without network access or reading stdin.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success; 2 for local validation errors; 22 for HTTP redirects and errors; other codes indicate transport failures. No automatic redirects, retries or pagination.
.SH SECURITY
Log content is untrusted and may contain sensitive data. Never expose tokens. Pixel GET submits data. Temp files used by shell/Lua are private and removed on handled exits.
.SH SEE ALSO
The repository README and skills/loggly references describe installation, completion and native APIs.
